+  `~/.pi/agent` (Spec environments §7.4, Decision 0017 choice 3). Existing
+  homes linked at the old `~/.pi/auth.json` target are reported detached,
+  never silently re-pointed; the move itself is an explicit migration step.
 
 ### Fixed
 
+- Credential-link repairs are fix-first and never destroy bytes (Spec
+  environments §7.4/§10.1, manager §12.4, Decision 0017). Repair unlinks
+  only a recorded symlink still targeting the declared native store; a
+  regular file, a symlink to an unexpected target, or a foreign link at a
+  link path refuses with `environment_credential_conflict` naming the path,
+  removing nothing — previously the path was unconditionally removed and
+  re-linked. A `shared`→`isolated` turn now removes the stale recorded
+  link instead of leaving sharing active behind an `isolated`
+  configuration, and `env status`/`env resolve` report a dangling or
+  mis-targeted recorded link as detached with conflict-class wording,
+  never silence — including a correctly targeted link whose native
+  target does not exist yet. Provisioning with no native credential yet
+  still succeeds, carrying the dangling state as a warning; later
+  resolves report it stale until the native side heals.
 - Git snapshots are extracted from the object database (`git ls-tree -r -z`
   plus `git cat-file --batch`) instead of `git archive`, so every regular file
   carries exactly its committed blob bytes. `git archive` applied
